# Everything by default; the builder copies what it needs explicitly.
#
# A deny-list here is how a secret reaches an image: somebody adds a file, nobody
# updates the ignore list, and it ships. Starting from "exclude everything" means a
# new file is absent from the image until a COPY names it.
*

# Source and manifests the build needs.
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!turbo.json
!apps
!packages
!infrastructure

# ...minus anything inside those trees that must never be in an image.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.next-e2e
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/.artifacts
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets and local state. Named explicitly as well as excluded by the `*` above,
# because this is the list somebody will read when asking "could a secret get in".
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
storage
.git
